ho is actively involved in the development of screening tools for undernutrition in geriatric practice. Their work focuses on addressing the critical issue of undernutrition among the elderly, contributing valuable insights and methodologies to improve the assessment and management of this condition in healthcare settings.GUIGOZ Y:Guigoz Y is a researcher and author who has conducted a thorough review of the literature on the Mini Nutritional Assessment. This assessment is recognized for its effectiveness in evaluating nutritional status, and Guigoz Y's work contributes to the understanding and application of this important tool in nutritional research.MC LAUGHLIN J:McLaughlin J is a researcher involved in the study of subjective global assessment of nutritional status.BAKER J:Baker J is a researcher who co-authored the study on subjective global assessment of nutritional status.ANEXO 2:Anexo 2 refers to a section in the document that provides tools for screening malnutrition and nutritional assessment.DESKY A:CRIBAGE:Cribage is a nutritional screening process assessing appetite, weight loss, mobility, and psychological stress over the past three months.EVALUACION:EvaluaciÃ³n is a follow-up assessment to determine the nutritional status of a patient based on various health indicators.APETITO:Apetito is a measure of the patient's desire to eat, which is assessed during the cribage process.COMIDAS:Comidas refers to the number of complete meals the patient consumes daily, which is assessed for nutritional evaluation.CIRCUNFERENCIA DE LA PANTORRILLA:Circunferencia de la pantorrilla is another measurement used to evaluate nutritional status and muscle mass.GERIATRIC PRACTICE:Geriatric practice involves the care of older adults, where tools like the MNA are utilized to assess nutritional status.STRATTON R:Stratton R is one of the authors of the malnutrition universal screening tool (MUST) and has contributed to the field of nutrition.LONGMORE D:Longmore D is a co-author o