¼¶1z»b[»`›§<{"title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF EATING DISORDERS:The International Journal of Eating Disorders publishes research on eating disorders and their treatment."}{"title": "FOOD CHEMISTRY:Food Chemistry is a journal that focuses on the chemistry and biochemistry of food."}{"title": "NUTRITION RESEARCH REVIEWS:Nutrition Research Reviews publishes reviews on various topics in nutrition research."}{"title": "INTERNATIONAL JOURNAL OF BEHAVIORAL NUTRITION AND PHYSICAL ACTIVITY:The International Journal of Behavioral Nutrition and Physical Activity focuses on the relationship between nutrition, physical activity, and health."}{"title": "JOURNAL OF NUTRITION:The Journal of Nutrition publishes original research and reviews in the field of nutrition."}{"title": "PROGRESS IN LIPID RESEARCH:"}{"title": "DR. GABRIEL OLVEIRA FUSTER:Dr. Gabriel Olveira Fuster is a medical professional involved in nutrition and health research."}{"title": "DR. JOS\u00c9 LUIS PEREIRA CUNILL:Dr. Jos\u00e9 Luis Pereira Cunill is a medical professional involved in nutrition and health research."}{"title": "PARENTERAL NUTRITION SOLUTIONS:Solutions for providing nutrition intravenously."}{"title": "ENTERAL FORMULAS:Oral enteral formulas commonly used in the medical field."}{"title": "MOBILE APPLICATIONS:Mobile applications for iPhone and Android useful in nutrition."}{"title": "GROWTH CHARTS:Spanish growth charts based on studies from 2010 for monitoring child growth."}{"title": "ENDOCRINOLOGY NUTRITION:Endocrinology Nutrition is a field of study focusing on the relationship between nutrition and endocrine health."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL EPIDEMIOLOGY:Nutritional Epidemiology is a field that studies the relationship between nutrition and health outcomes in populations."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL INTERVENTION PROGRAM:A community-based intervention program aimed at promoting healthy lifestyles among children and families."}{"title": "VARONES 19-30 A\u00d1OS:Varones 19-30 a\u00f1os refers to males aged 19-30 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "MUJERES 19-30 A\u00d1OS:Mujeres 19-30 a\u00f1os refers to females aged 19-30 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "M\u00c1S DE 70 A\u00d1OS:\"M\u00c1S DE 70 A\u00d1OS\" refers to individuals older than 70 years, a specific age group that is being assessed for nutritional status and potential malnutrition. This demographic is significant in dietary recommendations, as their nutritional needs may differ from those of younger populations."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS/AS 4-8 A\u00d1OS:Ni\u00f1os/as 4-8 a\u00f1os refers to children aged 4-8 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS/AS 9-13 A\u00d1OS:Ni\u00f1os/as 9-13 a\u00f1os refers to children aged 9-13 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "ADOLESCENTES 14-18 A\u00d1OS:Adolescentes 14-18 a\u00f1os refers to teenagers aged 14-18 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "ADULTOS 31-50 A\u00d1OS:Adultos 31-50 a\u00f1os refers to adults aged 31-50 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "ADULTOS 51-70 A\u00d1OS:Adultos 51-70 a\u00f1os refers to adults aged 51-70 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "LACTANCIA 19-30 A\u00d1OS:Lactancia 19-30 a\u00f1os refers to breastfeeding individuals aged 19-30 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "LACTANCIA 31-50 A\u00d1OS:Lactancia 31-50 a\u00f1os refers to breastfeeding individuals aged 31-50 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "LACTANCIA > 70 A\u00d1OS:Lactancia > 70 a\u00f1os refers to breastfeeding individuals older than 70 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "EMBARAZO 31-50 A\u00d1OS:Embarazo 31-50 a\u00f1os refers to pregnant individuals aged 31-50 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS/AS 4-18 A\u00d1OS:Ni\u00f1os/as 4-18 a\u00f1os refers to children aged 4-18 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS/AS 9-30 A\u00d1OS:Ni\u00f1os/as 9-30 a\u00f1os refers to children aged 9-30 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS/AS 14-18 A\u00d1OS:Ni\u00f1os/as 14-18 a\u00f1os refers to children aged 14-18 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS/AS 31-50 A\u00d1OS:Ni\u00f1os/as 31-50 a\u00f1os refers to children aged 31-50 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS/AS 51-70 A\u00d1OS:Ni\u00f1os/as 51-70 a\u00f1os refers to children aged 51-70 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS/AS > 70 A\u00d1OS:Ni\u00f1os/as > 70 a\u00f1os refers to children older than 70 years, a specific group in dietary recommendations."}{"title": "INGESTAS DIARIAS RECOMENDADAS:Ingestas diarias recomendadas (RDA) refer to the daily intake levels of essential nutrients that are recommended for various age groups and population groups. These guidelines are designed to ensure that individuals receive adequate nutrition to maintain health and prevent deficiencies."}{"title": "INGESTAS ADECUADAS:Ingestas adecuadas (AI) refer to the adequate intake levels of essential nutrients that are established for various population groups. These intake levels are particularly important in situations where the Recommended Dietary Allowance (RDA) cannot be determined. In essence, AIs serve as a guideline to ensure that individuals receive sufficient nutrients to maintain health and prevent deficiencies."}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS/AS 1-3 A\u00d1OS:"}{"title": "EMBARAZO 14-18 A\u00d1OS:"}{"title": "NI\u00d1OS/AS:The term \"Ni\u00f1os/as\" refers to children categorized by specific age groups for health and demographic statistics, encompassing those aged 1 to 19 years. More specifically, it includes children aged 1-3 years, 4-8 years, 9-13 years, and 14-18 years. This categorization is important for establishing dietary intake recommendations and guidelines, particularly concerning essential nutrients such as sodium and other minerals. Ni\u00f1os/as are also included in dietary reference intake guidelines, which provide tailored dietary recommendations to support their health and development during these critical growth stages."}{"title": "9-13 A\u00d1OS:The entity \"9-13 A\u00d1OS\" refers to the age group of preteens, specifically encompassing children aged 9 to 13 years old. This demographic is categorized for health and demographic statistics, which include specific dietary recommendations tailored to their developmental needs. Additionally, this age group is associated with various health metrics and developmental indicators that are crucial for understanding their growth and well-being."}{"title": "14-18 A\u00d1OS:The term \"14-18 a\u00f1os\" refers to the age group of teenagers, specifically encompassing individuals from 14 to 18 years old. This demographic is often categorized for health and demographic statistics, highlighting the unique developmental indicators and health metrics associated with this age range. Additionally, there are specific dietary recommendations tailored to meet the nutritional needs of teenagers within this group, ensuring their health and well-being during these formative years."}{"title": "19-30 A\u00d1OS:The entity \"19-30 A\u00d1OS\" refers to the age group of males aged 19 to 30 years old. This demographic is categorized for health and demographic statistics, and it includes associated health metrics relevant to this specific age range."}{"title": "31-50 A\u00d1OS:The entity \"31-50 A\u00d1OS\" refers to the age group of males aged 31 to 50 years old. This demographic is categorized for health and demographic statistics, and it includes associated health metrics relevant to this specific age range."}{"title": "51-70 A\u00d1OS:The entity \"51-70 A\u00d1OS\" refers to the age group of males aged between 51 and 70 years old. This demographic is categorized for health and demographic statistics, and it includes associated health metrics relevant to this specific age range."}{"title": ">70 A\u00d1OS:Refers to the age group of males over 70 years, with associated health metrics."}{"title": "9-13 A\u00d1OS MUJERES:Refers to the age group of females from 9 to 13 years, with associated health metrics."}{"title": "14-18 A\u00d1OS MUJERES:Refers to the age group of females from 14 to 18 years, with associated health metrics."}{"title": "19-30 A\u00d1OS MUJERES:Refers to the age group of females from 19 to 30 years, with associated health metrics."}{"title": "31-50 A\u00d1OS MUJERES:Refers to the age group of females from 31 to 50 years, with associated health metrics."}{"title": "51-70 A\u00d1OS MUJERES:Refers to the age group of females from 51 to 70 years, with associated health metrics."}{"title": ">70 A\u00d1OS MUJERES:Refers to the age group of females over 70 years, with associated health metrics."}{"title": "FLUOR:FLUOR, commonly known as fluoride, is a mineral recognized for its role in preventing dental cavities. It is essential for maintaining oral health, and its dietary reference intake is specified for various age groups in health guidelines. The recommended daily intake levels of fluoride are outlined in dietary guidelines to ensure adequate consumption for optimal health benefits."}{"title": "7-12 MESES:The term \"7-12 meses\" refers to the age group of infants aged 7 to 12 months. This period is characterized by specific dietary recommendations tailored to meet the nutritional needs of infants as they transition from exclusive breastfeeding or formula feeding to the introduction of solid foods. During this stage, it is essential to provide a balanced diet that supports growth and development, ensuring that infants receive the necessary nutrients for their health and well-being."}{"title": "> 70 A\u00d1OS:Age group of males older than 70 years, categorized for health and demographic statistics"}{"title": "9-13 A\u00d1OS (MUJERES):Age group of females from 9 to 13 years old, categorized for health and demographic statistics"}{"title": "14-18 A\u00d1OS (MUJERES):Age group of females from 14 to 18 years old, categorized for health and demographic statistics"}{"title": "19-30 A\u00d1OS (MUJERES):Age group of females from 19 to 30 years old, categorized for health and demographic statistics"}{"title": "31-50 A\u00d1OS (MUJERES):Age group of females from 31 to 50 years old, categorized for health and demographic statistics"}{"title": "51-70 A\u00d1OS (MUJERES):Age group of females from 51 to 70 years old, categorized for health and demographic statistics"}{"title": "> 70 A\u00d1OS (MUJERES):Age group of females older than 70 years, categorized for health and demographic statistics"}{"title": "DRI 971:DRI 971 is a document that outlines dietary reference intakes for various population groups."}{"title": "MOLYBDENUM:Molybdenum, also known as molibdeno, is a mineral that plays a crucial role in human nutrition. The dietary reference intake for molybdenum is specified for different age groups in established guidelines, ensuring that individuals receive appropriate amounts for their health needs. Recommended daily intake levels of molybdenum are outlined in these dietary guidelines, highlighting its importance in a balanced diet."}{"title": "NICKEL:N\u00edquel is nickel, a mineral with recommended daily intake levels outlined in the dietary guidelines."}{"title": "VANADIUM:Vanadio is vanadium, a mineral with recommended daily intake levels outlined in the dietary guidelines."}{"title": "ARSENIC:Ars\u00e9nico is arsenic, a mineral with recommended daily intake levels outlined in the dietary guidelines."}{"title": "SILICON:Silicio is silicon, a mineral with recommended daily intake levels outlined in the dietary guidelines."}{"title": "VARONES Y MUJERES:Varones y mujeres refers to adolescents aged 9-18 years, with specific dietary recommendations for sodium and other minerals."}{"title": "LIMITE SUPERIOR:L\u00edmite superior o UL refers to the maximum daily intake level of nutrients without probable adverse effects."}{"title": "INGESTA RECOMENDADA:Ingesta recomendada refers to the recommended intake levels of nutrients for different population groups."}{"title": "ACIDO PANTOTENICO:Pantothenic acid is a nutrient for which upper limits have not been established due to lack of data on adverse effects."}{"title": "CAROTENOIDES:Carotenoids are nutrients for which upper limits have not been established due to lack of data on adverse effects."}{"title": "ARSENICO:Arsenic is a nutrient for which upper limits have not been established due to lack of data on adverse effects."}{"title": "SILICIO:Silicon is a nutrient for which upper limits have not been established due to lack of data on adverse effects."}{"title": "GRUPO DE POBLACION:The term \"Grupo de poblaci\u00f3n\" refers to the demographic categories for which nutrient recommendations are established, encompassing various age groups and specific conditions. These population groups are defined by different age categories, each of which has specified nutrient intake levels to ensure adequate nutrition tailored to their needs."}{"title": "NINOS/AS:Ni\u00f1os/as refers to children aged 1-3 years for whom specific nutrient intake levels are defined."}{"title": "4-5 A\u00d1OS:Refers to the age group of children from 4 to 5 years, which has specific dietary intake recommendations."}{"title": "6-9 A\u00d1OS:Refers to the age group of children from 6 to 9 years, which has specific dietary intake recommendations."}{"title": "10-13 A\u00d1OS:The entity \"10-13 A\u00d1OS\" refers to the age group of children aged 10 to 13 years. This group has specific dietary intake recommendations tailored to their developmental needs and growth patterns."}{"title": "14-19 A\u00d1OS:The entity \"14-19 A\u00d1OS\" refers to a specific age group of adolescents ranging from 14 to 19 years old. This group is being assessed for nutritional status and potential malnutrition, highlighting the importance of understanding their dietary needs. There are specific dietary intake recommendations tailored for this age group, which are crucial for their growth and development during these formative years."}{"title": "20-29 A\u00d1OS:The entity \"20-29 A\u00d1OS\" refers to a specific age group of young adults, encompassing individuals aged 20 to 29 years. This demographic is being assessed for their nutritional status and potential malnutrition, highlighting the importance of understanding their dietary needs. Additionally, there are specific dietary intake recommendations tailored for this age group, aimed at promoting optimal health and well-being during these formative years of adulthood."}{"title": "30-39 A\u00d1OS:The entity \"30-39 A\u00d1OS\" refers to a specific age group of adults aged 30 to 39 years. This demographic is being assessed for nutritional status and potential malnutrition, highlighting the importance of understanding their dietary needs. Additionally, there are specific dietary intake recommendations tailored for this age group to ensure optimal health and nutrition."}{"title": "40-49 A\u00d1OS:The entity \"40-49 A\u00d1OS\" refers to a specific age group of adults aged 40 to 49 years. This demographic is being assessed for nutritional status and potential malnutrition, highlighting the importance of understanding their dietary needs. Additionally, there are specific dietary intake recommendations tailored for this age group to ensure optimal health and nutrition."}{"title": "50-59 A\u00d1OS:The entity \"50-59 A\u00d1OS\" refers to a specific age group of adults aged 50 to 59 years. This demographic is being assessed for nutritional status and potential malnutrition, highlighting the importance of understanding their dietary needs. Additionally, there are specific dietary intake recommendations tailored for this age group to ensure optimal health and nutrition."}{"title": "60-69 A\u00d1OS:The entity \"60-69 A\u00d1OS\" refers to a specific age group of older adults, encompassing individuals aged 60 to 69 years. This demographic is being assessed for their nutritional status and potential malnutrition, highlighting the importance of understanding their dietary needs. There are specific dietary intake recommendations tailored for this age group to ensure their nutritional requirements are met effectively."}{"title": "70 A\u00d1OS:Refers to the age group of older adults aged 70 years and above, which has specific dietary intake recommendations."}{"title": "RUBENSTEIN LZ:Rubenstein LZ is a researcher and author who is actively involved in the development of screening tools for undernutrition in geriatric practice. Their work focuses on addressing the critical issue of undernutrition among the elderly, contributing valuable insights and methodologies to improve the assessment and management of this condition in healthcare settings."}{"title": "GUIGOZ Y:Guigoz Y is a researcher and author who has conducted a thorough review of the literature on the Mini Nutritional Assessment. This assessment is recognized for its effectiveness in evaluating nutritional status, and Guigoz Y's work contributes to the understanding and application of this important tool in nutritional research."}{"title": "MC LAUGHLIN J:McLaughlin J is a researcher involved in the study of subjective global assessment of nutritional status."}{"title": "BAKER J:Baker J is a researcher who co-authored the study on subjective global assessment of nutritional status."}{"title": "ANEXO 2:Anexo 2 refers to a section in the document that provides tools for screening malnutrition and nutritional assessment."}{"title": "DESKY A:"}{"title": "CRIBAGE:Cribage is a nutritional screening process assessing appetite, weight loss, mobility, and psychological stress over the past three months."}{"title": "EVALUACION:Evaluaci\u00f3n is a follow-up assessment to determine the nutritional status of a patient based on various health indicators."}{"title": "APETITO:Apetito is a measure of the patient's desire to eat, which is assessed during the cribage process."}{"title": "COMIDAS:Comidas refers to the number of complete meals the patient consumes daily, which is assessed for nutritional evaluation."}{"title": "CIRCUNFERENCIA DE LA PANTORRILLA:Circunferencia de la pantorrilla is another measurement used to evaluate nutritional status and muscle mass."}{"title": "GERIATRIC PRACTICE:Geriatric practice involves the care of older adults, where tools like the MNA are utilized to assess nutritional status."}{"title": "STRATTON R:Stratton R is one of the authors of the malnutrition universal screening tool (MUST) and has contributed to the field of nutrition."}{"title": "LONGMORE D:Longmore D is a co-author of the malnutrition universal screening tool (MUST) and has expertise in clinical nutrition."}{"title": "FERGUSON M:Ferguson M is an author who developed a valid and reliable malnutrition screening tool for adult acute hospital patients."}{"title": "NUTRITION 1999:A publication that discusses the development of a valid and reliable malnutrition screening tool for adult acute hospital patients."}{"title": "FIGHT MALNUTRITION:Fight Malnutrition is an organization focused on combating malnutrition through various initiatives and tools."}{"title": "SCREENING TOOL:A screening tool is a method used to identify individuals at risk of malnutrition, such as MUST and SNAQ."}{"title": "NUTRITION 2003:"}{"title": "EMGO+:The EMGO+ Institute is involved in the development of nutritional screening tools and collaborates with various health organizations."}{"title": "MINISTERIO HOLAND\u00c9S DE SALUD Y BIENESTAR:The Dutch Ministry of Health and Welfare provides funding and support for health-related initiatives, including malnutrition research."}{"title": "VU UNIVERSITY:VU University is an academic institution that collaborates with the EMGO+ Institute on health research projects."}{"title": "SNAQ65+:SNAQ65+ is a nutritional screening tool developed to assess the risk of malnutrition in older adults."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL RISK REPORT:The Nutritional Risk Report is a document that evaluates and classifies the risk of malnutrition based on various health parameters."}{"title": "CONUT:CONUT is a scoring system used to assess nutritional risk based on specific health parameters."}{"title": "NUTRITION SUPPORT TEAM:The Nutrition Support Team is a group of healthcare professionals that provides nutritional care and support to patients."}{"title": "ENDOCRINOLOGY AND NUTRITION CLINIC:The Endocrinology and Nutrition Clinic is a medical facility that specializes in the treatment of endocrine disorders and nutritional issues."}{"title": "PHARMACY:The Pharmacy is a healthcare facility that provides medications and may collaborate with the Nutrition Support Team for patient care."}{"title": "NUTRITIONAL RISK ASSESSMENT:Nutritional Risk Assessment is a process used to evaluate an individual's risk of malnutrition based on various health indicators."}{"title": "EQUIPO DE SOPORTE NUTRICIONAL:The Nutritional Support Team (ESN) is responsible for providing nutritional support and care in a clinical setting."}{"title": "U.G.C DE ENDOCRINOLOG\u00cdA Y NUTRICI\u00d3N CL\u00cdNICA:The Clinical Endocrinology and Nutrition Unit (U.G.C) specializes in the diagnosis and treatment of nutritional disorders."}{"title": "U.G.C. FARMACIA:The Pharmacy Unit (U.G.C) is involved in the management and provision of medications and nutritional supplements."}{"title": "VILLALOBOS J. L.:J. L. Villalobos is a researcher involved in the validation of nutritional screening processes in hospitals."}{"title": "GARC\u00cdA-ALMEIDA J. M.:J. M. Garc\u00eda-Almeida is a researcher who co-authored studies on nutritional assessment and screening methods."}{"title": "SUJETOS ADULTOS SANOS:Grupo de sujetos adultos sanos con IMC entre 18,5 y 40 kg/m\u00b2 que fueron estudiados"}{"title": "SUJETOS ESTUDIADOS:N\u00famero total de sujetos que participaron en el estudio, con datos presentados en las tablas"}{"title": "PIZARRA:Pizarra is a location in M\u00e1laga, Spain, where the population percentiles for the Jamar dynamometer were studied."}{"title": "JAMAR DYNAMOMETER:The Jamar dynamometer is a tool used for measuring grip strength, with population percentiles established in Pizarra."}{"title": "GROUP UNDER 45 YEARS:A group of subjects under 45 years old studied for grip strength measurement."}{"title": "GROUP BETWEEN 45 AND 60 YEARS:A group of subjects aged between 45 and 60 years studied for grip strength measurement."}{"title": "GROUP OVER 60 YEARS:A group of subjects over 60 years old studied for grip strength measurement."}{"title": "ADULT SUBJECTS:"}{"title": "VAMIN\u00ae 14:Vamin\u00ae 14 is a nitrogen solution used for parenteral nutrition, containing amino acids and nitrogen for adult patients."}{"title": "SINTAMIN\u00ae 17:Sinthamin\u00ae 17 is a nitrogen solution for parenteral nutrition, providing essential amino acids and nitrogen."}{"title": "AMINO-PLASMA\u00ae L-15:Amino-Plasmal\u00ae L-15 is a parenteral nitrogen solution rich in amino acids, used for nutritional support."}{"title": "TAURAMIN:Tauramin is a nitrogen solution for parenteral nutrition that includes taurine and amino acids."}{"title": "AMINO-PLASMA\u00ae PO 10:Amino-Plasmal\u00ae PO 10 is a parenteral nutrition solution with a high concentration of amino acids."}{"title": "GLAMIN\u00ae:Glamin\u00ae is a nitrogen solution for parenteral nutrition, known for its high glutamine content."}{"title": "NEPHROMINE\u00ae 5,4%:Nephromine\u00ae 5,4% is a specialized nitrogen solution for parenteral nutrition, designed for patients with renal issues."}{"title": "AMINOSTERIL\u00ae N-HEPA 8%:Aminosteril\u00ae N-Hepa 8% is a nitrogen solution for parenteral nutrition, formulated for patients with liver conditions."}{"title": "DIPEPTIVEN\u00ae:Dipeptiven\u00ae is a nitrogen solution for parenteral nutrition that contains dipeptides for enhanced absorption."}{"title": "INTRALIPID\u00ae 30%:Intralipid\u00ae 30% is a lipid solution used for parenteral nutrition, primarily composed of soybean oil."}{"title": "INTRALIPID\u00ae 20%:Intralipid\u00ae 20% is a lipid solution for parenteral nutrition, providing essential fatty acids from soybean oil."}{"title": "CLINOLEIC\u00ae 20%:Clinoleic\u00ae 20% is a lipid solution for parenteral nutrition, containing a blend of oleic and soybean oils."}{"title": "LIPOFUNDINA\u00ae 10%:Lipofundina\u00ae 10% is a lipid solution for parenteral nutrition, made from medium-chain triglycerides and soybean oil."}{"title": "LIPOFUNDINA\u00ae 20%:Lipofundina\u00ae 20% is a lipid solution for parenteral nutrition, providing a higher concentration of medium-chain triglycerides."}{"title": "LIPOPLUS\u00ae 20%:Lipoplus\u00ae 20% is a lipid solution for parenteral nutrition, containing a mix of medium-chain triglycerides, soybean oil, and omega-3 fatty acids."}{"title": "SMOFLIPID\u00ae 20%:SMOFlipid\u00ae 20% is a lipid solution for parenteral nutrition, combining multiple lipid sources including omega-3 fatty acids."}{"title": "OMEGAVEN\u00ae:Omegaven\u00ae is a lipid solution for parenteral nutrition, rich in omega-3 fatty acids, used for patients requiring specialized nutrition."}{"title": "SOLUCIONES LIP\u00cdDICAS:Soluciones lip\u00eddicas are parenteral nutrition solutions that provide essential fatty acids for patients requiring nutritional support."}{"title": "SOLUCIONES NITROGENADAS:"}{"title": "ISOPLASMAL G:Isoplasmal G is a commercial nitrogen solution used for hypocaloric peripheral parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "AMINOVEN 3,5%:Aminoven 3,5% is a commercial amino acid solution used for hypocaloric peripheral parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "NUTRIFLEX LIPID:NuTRIflex Lipid is a brand of parenteral nutrition products that includes various formulations for different nutritional needs."}{"title": "SOLUCIONES NITROGENADAS Y LIP\u00cdDICAS:SOLUCIONES NITROGENADAS Y LIP\u00cdDICAS refers to specific formulations designed for parenteral nutrition, which is a method of delivering essential nutrients directly into the bloodstream for patients who are unable to consume food orally. These solutions are crucial for providing nitrogen and lipids, which are vital components necessary for maintaining the nutritional needs of individuals who cannot receive nutrition through the digestive tract."}{"title": "TABLA 4A:Tabla 4A details the manufacturer Braun's products related to parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "NP PERIF\u00c9RICA HIPOCAL\u00d3RICA:NP perif\u00e9rica hipocal\u00f3rica refers to a type of parenteral nutrition that is low in calories."}{"title": "KABIVEN CENTRAL:Kabiven Central is a product line from Fresenius Kabi that provides a specific formulation for parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "KABIVEN PERIFERICO:Kabiven Perif\u00e9rico is another product line from Fresenius Kabi designed for peripheral parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "OLIGOPLUS:Oligoplus is a product from Fresenius Kabi used as an additive in parenteral nutrition solutions."}{"title": "OLIGOSTANDARD:Oligostandard is another additive product from Fresenius Kabi for parenteral nutrition."}{"title": "SMOFKABIVEN CENTRAL:SmofKabiven Central is a product offered by Fresenius Kabi, designed for parenteral nutrition with specific nutrient compositions."}{"title": "SMOFKABIVEN:SmofKabiven is a nutritional product available in central presentations without electrolytes."}{"title": "OLICLINOMEL:Oliclinomel is a nutritional solution offered in various formulations for peripheral and central administration."}{"title": "ADDITIVOS:Additivos refer to various substances added to nutritional solutions to enhance stability and nutritional value."}{"title": "FRESUBIN PROTEIN ENERGY DRINK:Fresubin Protein Energy Drink is a nutritional supplement produced by Fresenius Kabi, offered in multiple flavors and aimed at providing energy and protein for patients."}{"title": "FRESUBIN 2 KCAL DRINK:Fresubin 2 kcal Drink is a high-calorie nutritional product from Fresenius Kabi, designed to support patients requiring additional caloric intake."}{"title": "FRESUBIN 2 KCAL FIBRE DRINK:Fresubin 2 kcal Fibre Drink is a nutritional supplement by Fresenius Kabi that provides high calories and fiber, suitable for patients needing dietary support."}{"title": "PRODUCT:"}{"title": "DIETGRIF PUDDING COMPLETO:Dietgrif Pudding Completo is a nutritional product offered by Grifols, available in various flavors such as Vanilla, Caramel, and Chocolate."}{"title": "DIETGRIF ACTIV PROTEIN FIBRA:Dietgrif Activ Protein Fibra is a protein-rich drink produced by Grifols, available in flavors like Strawberry and Vanilla."}{"title": "RENUTRYL:Renutryl is a nutritional drink produced by Nestl\u00e9, available in flavors such as Vanilla, Strawberry, and Coffee."}{"title": "RESOURCE 2.0:Resource 2.0 is a nutritional drink by Nestl\u00e9, available in flavors like Vanilla and Apricot."}{"title": "RESOURCE 2.0 FIBRA:Resource 2.0 Fibra is a fiber-rich nutritional drink from Nestl\u00e9, available in various flavors including Soft Vanilla and Forest Fruits."}{"title": "RESOURCE 2.0 SHOT:Resource 2.0 Shot is a compact nutritional drink by Nestl\u00e9, available in flavors like Vanilla and Coffee."}{"title": "RESOURCE HP/HC:Resource HP/HC is a high-protein nutritional drink from Nestl\u00e9, available in flavors like Vanilla, Chocolate, and Strawberry."}{"title": "RESOURCE SENIOR ACTIV:Resource Senior Activ is a nutritional drink by Nestl\u00e9 designed for seniors, available in flavors like Vanilla and Caramel."}{"title": "FORTIMEL COMPACT:Fortimel Compact is a nutritional drink produced by Nutricia, available in flavors like Vanilla and Strawberry."}{"title": "FORTIMEL COMPLETE:Fortimel Complete is a comprehensive nutritional drink produced by Nutricia, designed to meet complete dietary needs. It is available in a variety